 6. 🖊 New White House counsel 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Will Scharf tees up executive orders for President Trump in the Oval Office last year. Photo: Al Drago/Bloomberg via Getty Images Longtime Trump aide Will Scharf, now the White House staff secretary, will take over as the next White House counsel on Sept. 1, the White House announced last night. 

 Scharf replaces Dave Warrington, who'll leave the administration for the private sector. Scharf represented Trump in his Supreme Court presidential-immunity case.

 Scharf chairs the National Capital Planning Commission, which has tried to clear the way for Trump's White House ballroom construction. An appellate court halted the project Friday. 
 
