 8. 🤖 1 for the road: GTA meets GPTs 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 A shot from a created video game. Photo: Matt Shumer/X 

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The reality of building your own video game is here. And just like so many other AI-driven changes, it threatens to permanently disrupt a $300 billion industry, Axios' Herb Scribner reports .

 Gamers on X are posting videos of playable game demos built using LLMs, many of them resembling popular shooters like "Call of Duty" and "Counter-Strike." "If something is kind of possible today, in a year, it's going to be nailed," Matt Shumer, an AI investor and video game builder, told Axios. Share this story . 

 
 
